rationale:
The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`.

**Exactly one argument, `result`.** `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` checks the `submit_result` parameter schema. It asserts `required == ["result"]`, `additionalProperties == false`, and that `properties` has exactly one entry. It also submits four bad calls and expects `ValidationError::Agent` each time, without reaching vetting:
- a wrongly typed `result`;
- empty arguments;
- an `other` field with no `result`;
- `result` plus an `extra` field.

The last case directly exercises the "exactly one argument" rule.

**Schema derived from `R: JsonSchema` via schemars.** Two result types are checked:
- For `bool`, `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` asserts `schema.properties.result.type == "boolean"`.
- For the struct `Answer`, `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors` asserts a `$defs/Decision` entry and a `$ref` of `#/$defs/Decision` under `properties.result.properties.decision`.

The same schema reaches real backend wire formats. `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` asserts `parameters.required == ["result"]` and `result.type == "boolean"` in the OpenAI request. `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` asserts `function.parameters.required == ["result"]` in the Ollama request. `submit_result` is also checked as the last tool in the fixed tool list.

**Accepted call ends the conversation.** The tests show that a `submit_result` call returns the decoded answer:
- the typed test yields `Decision::Yes`;
- the scalar test yields `true`;
- the Ollama test yields `true` after exactly 2 requests;
- the OpenAI test makes exactly 4 requests across 2 independent runs, 2 per run, so no further model turn follows acceptance.

The acceptance details (search-page gating, skipping other calls, vetting) belong to `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.acceptance`. This requirement only cites that one, so those details need no test here.

No gaps found. All the tests carry `{test}` markers for the subject.
